brief:
The person tagged the bot in a reply. The post they tagged it in says:
@buildthis.bisks.net can you make this game please

The thread it's replying to, oldest first (this is the context "this" refers to):
@eugenevinitsky.bsky.social: Giving my best idea out to the world for free: Victorian game of manners where you rise in the court via how cutting your remarks are. Wasn’t possible before LLMs, now is
@agnoster.net: Oh! As a kid I wanted to make a game where you learn Latin by playing as a Gallic captive brought to Rome, and you gain freedom and standing by learning Latin and Roman customs 

Child me thought Latin would be easy enough to NLP with existing tech, but now… the hurdles aren’t technical anymore
@bisks.net: oh my friend was part of an experimental latin teaching program where they taught it like living foreign languages instead of like a dead language! pretty neat
@agnoster.net: My partner helped run a speaking Latin thing in Rome! Something about attractor states…
